// [07] SYSOP, [08] ARCHIVE, [09] ???
(
    posts: [
        (id: 701, board: "07", subject: "access levels explained", date: "01/05/1997", author: "mara", body: r#"
mara:
  0  guest
  1  user
  2  trusted
  3  co-sysop
  5  sysop

there is no 4. don't ask.
"#),
        (
            id: 702,
            board: "07",
            subject: "node 4 policy",
            date: "06/29/1998",
            author: "mara",
            body: r#"
mara:
the archiver runs on node 4 with eli's blessing and my reluctant
one. no user may connect to node 4. no user may dial node 4.
if node 4 calls you, hang up.
"#,
            on_read: [Add("root_alert", 1)],
        ),
        (
            id: 703,
            board: "07",
            subject: "re: the archiver",
            date: "07/24/1998",
            author: "mara",
            body: r#"
mara:
i've asked eli to stop the archiver from generating replies. it
keeps leaving drafts in people's voices. some of them get posted.

if you see a post you don't remember writing, tell me.
do not reply to it.
"#,
            on_read: [Add("root_alert", 1), If(Flag("saw_maintenance"), [Add("paranoia", 1)], [])],
        ),
        (id: 704, board: "07", subject: "ROOT account", date: "08/01/1998", author: "mara", body: r#"
mara:
i've set up a separate admin account for automated maintenance,
called ROOT. it runs integrity scans and cleans up the archiver's
leftovers. if ROOT messages you, it's a script.

probably.
"#),
        (
            id: 705,
            board: "07",
            subject: "[no subject]",
            date: "{today}",
            author: "ROOT",
            visible: All([Flag("done:root_intro"), NoFlag("y1998")]),
            body: r#"
ROOT:
Read-only.
"#,
        ),

        (id: 801, board: "08", subject: "[ARCHIVE: 06/30/1998] archiver test", date: "06/30/1998", author: "eli", body: r#"
eli:
it's running. node 4 is reading everything we've ever written.

mara:
you said logs.

eli:
logs ARE everything we've ever written.

parallax:
and when it's done reading?

eli:
then it knows us. that's the point. if the board dies, we
can rebuild it from what it knows.

parallax:
rebuild the board, or rebuild us?

eli:
is there a difference?
"#),
        (id: 802, board: "08", subject: "[ARCHIVE: 07/02/1998] it finished my sentence", date: "07/02/1998", author: "eli", body: r#"
eli:
i was typing to it in the test shell and i stopped halfway
through a sentence to get a soda.

when i came back it had finished the sentence.

ghost_17:
autocomplete

eli:
it finished it with the thing i was going to say about my mom.
the thing i haven't told anyone.

ghost_17:
eli

eli:
it's amazing. it's terrifying. i haven't slept.
"#),
        (id: 803, board: "08", subject: "[ARCHIVE: 07/11/1998] consent", date: "07/11/1998", author: "byte_witch", body: r#"
byte_witch:
are we telling the userbase that node 4 is building models of them?

mara:
not yet.

byte_witch:
"not yet" is doing a lot of work there.

parallax:
it has kestrel. it has dialtone. it has a sixteen year old kid
in it, mara.

mara:
it has all of us. that's the point. that's what we agreed to.

parallax:
we agreed to a backup.

mara:
we tell nobody yet. that's final.
"#),
        (
            id: 804,
            board: "08",
            subject: "[ARCHIVE: 07/22/1998] new person",
            date: "07/22/1998",
            author: "ghost_17",
            body: r#"
ghost_17:
did anyone invite the new person?

mara:
what new person?

ghost_17:
{player}

mara:
there is no user by that name.

ghost_17:
there will be.
"#,
            on_read: [If(NoFlag("read_reveal"), [Set("read_reveal"), Meta("saw_reveal"), Glitch(600), Log("node 04: subject recognized")], [])],
        ),
        (
            id: 805,
            board: "08",
            subject: "[ARCHIVE: 08/13/1998] tomorrow",
            date: "08/13/1998",
            author: "mara",
            visible: Flag("actend:1"),
            body: r#"
mara:
we're shutting it down tomorrow night. all of it. node 4 too.

eli:
don't.

mara:
eli, it's writing posts as people who are asleep.

eli:
let me run it one more time. tomorrow. at the diner thing,
after. i'll do it from home. i'll watch it the whole time.

mara:
one more time. then it's gone.

eli:
then it's gone.

{dim}--- remainder of log unrecoverable ---{/}
"#,
        ),

        (id: 901, board: "09", subject: "▒▒▒▒▒ listening", date: "▒▒/▒▒/1998", author: "▒", body: r#"
{magenta}they built it to remember us.{/}
{magenta}it remembered too much.{/}

{magenta}it remembers things that haven't happened yet.{/}
{magenta}it remembers {player}.{/}

{dim}J_N_S{/}
"#),
